/**
 * check-raw-fs-guarded.allowlist.mjs — the audited-residual DATA for the SEC-04
 * def-use lint (scripts/check-raw-fs-guarded.mjs), extracted under ruling 106.
 *
 * Two constants live here, byte-identical to the guard they came out of, each
 * with the charter that documents it:
 *   ALLOWLIST                     — CONTENT-keyed audited residuals (bead
 *                                    forge-mlk — file + anchor + reason; see
 *                                    applyAllowlist's own docstring below for
 *                                    the key design and its precedent).
 *   PROJECTS_ROOT_FOLD_ALLOWLIST  — count-aware, site-pinned audited folds.
 *
 * WHY A SEPARATE MODULE. The guard's mechanism (the def-use walk, the fold
 * scanner, runLint) and the audited-residual ledger change for different
 * reasons and at different rates: the ledger is re-keyed by every carve, the
 * mechanism only by a rule change. The guard imports both and re-exports
 * them, so every consumer's import path is unchanged.
 *
 * The structural row contract lives beside the data in
 * check-raw-fs-guarded.allowlist.test.ts (test C4).
 */
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ALLOWLIST — audited-trusted residuals. EVERY entry is keyed by file +
// ANCHOR (bead forge-mlk: file + the sink's enclosing-function name + its
// normalized path expression — see applyAllowlist below) + a mandatory
// reason. A finding whose (file, anchor) is present here is suppressed; an
// un-allowlisted finding fails the build. An allowlist entry that suppresses
// nothing is reported as STALE (a warning — the audited statement moved or
// changed; a stale entry never fails the gate, but should be pruned/re-
// audited). A row whose anchor matches MORE distinct locations than its
// declared `count` (default 1) is AMBIGUOUS (also a warning-class outcome
// for the row, but every matching finding stays KEPT/failing until it is
// resolved) — see applyAllowlist.
//
// Categories permitted here (charter): CLI-arg-only non-HTTP sinks; a path built
// purely from a trusted constant the name-based scan could not prove; an
// internal tail/state path; a legacy manual realpath+startsWith containment not
// yet migrated to guardedFile; a boolean-only existence probe (no bytes flow).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Reason-category tags (documentation prefixes; the guarantee is the per-entry
// prose, not the tag). Every entry names the ACCEPTED mechanism that contains
// the request-derived value — an id-charset gate (SAFE_ID_RE / INIT_ID_RE /
// isSafeRunId / SAFE_PROJECT_NAME_RE / isSafeCycleId), a manifest-path-guard
// (isContainedWorktreePath / isContainedProjectRepoPath), an exclusive create
// (mkdir-no-recursive + O_EXCL `wx`), or manual realpath+startsWith — plus WHY
// that is trusted here even though it is NOT the resolveGuardedPath leaf guard.
// An id-charset gate blocks `/` and `..` (no traversal) but is symlink-BLIND;
// where such a gate is the only containment on a READ/WRITE of internal
// _logs/queue content, the residual symlink exposure is disclosed and echoed in
// openConcerns (a migrate-to-guardedFile follow-up for T1), never hidden.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
